                <pb facs="0071" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg21"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tripp to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    your information, copies of correspondence between this legation, the United
                    States consul at Budapest, and the ministry of foreign affairs at Vienna,
                    relative to the arrest, enrollment into the army and subsequent release of Mike
                    Minis, or Michael Minich, a native of the province of Slavonia, in the Kingdom
                    of Hungary, and a naturalized citizen of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bartlett Tripp.</hi></signed></closer>







